      "id": "21463206",
      "title": "v-bind and v-on Shorthands",
      "lectureOrder": 34,
      "videoOrder": 30,
      "sourceHash": "2c2d1da66cf5d9851d4dcda68c44fe42e859339fc9bafb441b22400ec1fa38f8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So now, it's almost time to practice again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "but here's what important shorthand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 9.39,
          "en": "one way of writing a bit shorter code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.39,
          "end": 10.98,
          "en": "which you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.98,
          "end": 14.27,
          "en": "Not directly related to computed properties and watchers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.27,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "but to view in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "We used v-on quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 22.39,
          "en": "and before we also used v-bind, if you remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.39,
          "end": 25.49,
          "en": "Now, v-on and v-bind are so common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.49,
          "end": 28.78,
          "en": "that there are shorthands for them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.78,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "Instead of using v-on:click, v-on:click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "v-on:input and whatever you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 38.83,
          "en": "You can replace v-on colon, with an at symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.83,
          "end": 40.58,
          "en": "And that's exactly the same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.58,
          "end": 43.96,
          "en": "It's just a shorthand provided by view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.96,
          "end": 46.653,
          "en": "to make adding event listeners a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 50.32,
          "en": "You can still combine this with modifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.32,
          "end": 52.82,
          "en": "and still do everything you did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.82,
          "end": 56.66,
          "en": "you just replace v-on colon with @,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.66,
          "end": 59.29,
          "en": "so that you have less code to write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.29,
          "end": 61.63,
          "en": "It's up to you if you want to use that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.63,
          "end": 63.72,
          "en": "you just should be consistent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.72,
          "end": 68.23,
          "en": "So if you do use it, use it for all events, not just some.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.23,
          "end": 70.52,
          "en": "And I'm going to use it throughout the course, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.52,
          "end": 72.993,
          "en": "But you don't have to, it's just an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.91,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "We also have a shortcut for v-bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "If we had v-bind:value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 84.1,
          "en": "then we can actually also just omit v-bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.1,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "and just have colon value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 89.23,
          "en": "for binding an attribute dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.23,
          "end": 91.78,
          "en": "So just colon, attribute name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.78,
          "end": 95.22999999999999,
          "en": "is a shorthand for v-bind colon attribute name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.22999999999999,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "and @event name is a shortcut for a v-on colon event name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.62,
          "end": 103.78,
          "en": "Again, it's up to you, what you prefer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.78,
          "end": 105.31,
          "en": "but you should be consistent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.31,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "and I'm going to use these shorthands throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 111.10300000000001,
          "en": "There is no v-model shorthand, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
